<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Statutes of Kilkenny</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1366</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Statutes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilkenny">Kilkenny</a> were laws passed by a parliament at Kilkenny in 1366 under Lionel of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a>, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glarentza">Clarence</a>. Aimed at the English settlers of the Lordship of Ireland, they forbade marriage with the Irish, the use of the Irish language and Brehon law, and other Gaelic customs. They reflected the shrinking of English rule in the face of a Gaelic revival and proved largely unenforceable.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/statutes-of-kilkenny.jpg" alt="Statutes of Kilkenny" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NsMn · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_Lordship_of_Ireland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
